      en: "Gazipur, located on the northern outskirts of Dhaka, is a rapidly growing industrial and administrative city. It is a vital part of the Greater Dhaka area and hosts a vast concentration of readymade garment (RMG) factories, making it a critical contributor to the national economy. Gazipur is also known for its diverse educational and research institutions, including several universities and the Islamic University of Technology. One of the city's most famous attractions is the Bangabandhu Sheikh Mujib Safari Park, the first of its kind in Bangladesh. The Bhawal National Park, a large forest area dominated by Sal trees, provides a green lung for the region and a popular spot for weekend getaways. Gazipur's strategic location on the highways connecting Dhaka to the northern and eastern parts of the country makes it a major transport hub. Geography K7 — Industrialization and Suburban Growth."
